[thin] These broad curved-skin rankings sample the analytic 3 mm inward offset of the outer rounded envelope. The STL uses 0.03 mm chord tolerance; the reported 2.995 and 2.996 mm runs differ from the exact offset by less than 0.006 mm. Local tangent additions and the rim backing add material outside this ordinary stock. The ranking does not establish strength or whole-part surface performance.
alternatives: A 4 mm shell adds material across the entire compact envelope without changing the selected local radii or their printing orientation. Enlarging the body to retain a larger cavity defeats the compact reference. Increasing wall count is a separate print recipe and does not correct a geometric offset that already supplies 3 mm stock.
