[thin] These two 3.000 mm rankings read the fixed capture-lip stock from its Z7.40 underside to its Z10.40 top. The adjoining guide walls root the lips; the moving shoulders below them retain 0.48 mm release air. The lips retain the moving member geometrically throughout the 10 mm stroke, with physical release and retention still unmeasured.
alternatives: A 4 mm lip adds stock above the same release surface without changing initial deposition or the intended fit. Thickening downward consumes release air and changes the single variation being printed. Enlarging the lip overlap also reduces the handle opening without adding a selected finish feature.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/arch-body.step
