[thin] These two 3.000 mm rankings read the connected ordinary floor from Z0 to Z3, including its interface to the local front stock. This floor roots the fixed guide and stop stock; the moving foot corridors are separate cuts. The thicker central running plinth has its own Z3.08 datum.
alternatives: Thickening the whole floor above Z3 adds material outside the running plinth and reduces the open cavity. Extending it beneath Z0 changes the bed datum and requires translating the complete mechanism. A separate thick base adds bulk without a further calibration reading.
